# Switch sessions

`--switch` should share create semantics, then switch the invoking tmux client
to the strictly resolved target and print its actual session name.

    :bins jj tmux cat sh sed

> [!NOTE]
> 'jj', 'tmux', 'cat', 'sh', and 'sed' are available.

    :copy tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)

    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :$ jj git init alpha (exit: 0)
    :$ jj describe -R alpha -m "base commit" (exit: 0)
    :$ jj workspace add -R alpha --name feature alpha.feature (exit: 0)
    :$ jj workspace add -R alpha --name other alpha.other (exit: 0)

Create a live feature session with agent attention in its second window. A
named-workspace base with no operand should infer `feature`, and switching to an
existing live target should select its first attention window. Stdout should
contain only the session name, not the window target.

    :t new-session -d -s feature-live -c alpha.feature "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -F -t '=feature-live:' @smth.repo '#{pane_start_path}' (success)
    :t new-window -d -t feature-live:1 -c alpha.feature "cat" (success)
    :t set-option -p -t feature-live:1.0 @smth.agent.state waiting (success)
    :t respawn-pane -k -t runner:0.0 'smth --base alpha.feature --switch > switch-name; tmux wait-for -S switched-feature; cat' (success)
    :t wait-for switched-feature (success)
    :$ cat switch-name (exit: 0)

```stdout
feature-live
```

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}:#{window_index}' (success)

```
feature-live:1
```

A default checkout with no live session should get one before the client
switches. A colliding plain session should force a disambiguated name in both
stdout and the selected client session.

    :t switch-client -t runner (success)
    :pane runner:0.0
    :t new-session -d -s alpha "cat" (success)
    :t respawn-pane -k -t runner:0.0 'smth --base alpha --switch > switch-name; tmux wait-for -S switched-default; cat' (success)
    :t wait-for switched-default (success)
    :$ cat switch-name (exit: 0)

```stdout
alpha~1
```

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}:#{window_index}' (success)

```
alpha~1:0
```

An explicit operand overrides the workspace inferred by a named base. Existing
checkouts receive tmux sessions without creating new workspaces.

    :t switch-client -t runner (success)
    :pane runner:0.0
    :t respawn-pane -k -t runner:0.0 'smth --base alpha.feature --switch other > switch-name; tmux wait-for -S switched-other; cat' (success)
    :t wait-for switched-other (success)
    :$ cat switch-name (exit: 0)

```stdout
alpha/other
```

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}:#{window_index}' (success)

```
alpha/other:0
```

A missing named workspace should be created at `--onto`, then switched to.

    :t switch-client -t runner (success)
    :pane runner:0.0
    :t respawn-pane -k -t runner:0.0 'smth --base alpha --onto @ --switch fresh > switch-name; tmux wait-for -S switched-fresh; cat' (success)
    :t wait-for switched-fresh (success)
    :$ cat switch-name (exit: 0)

```stdout
alpha/fresh
```

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}:#{window_index}' (success)

```
alpha/fresh:0
```

    :t switch-client -t runner (success)
    :pane runner:0.0
    :$ sh -c 'jj workspace list -R alpha --ignore-working-copy --no-pager --color never --template "name ++ \"\\n\"" | sed -n "/fresh/p"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
fresh
```

Plain targets should be created in the empty base namespace and switched to in
the same way.

    :t respawn-pane -k -t runner:0.0 'smth --no-base --switch scratch > switch-name; tmux wait-for -S switched-scratch; cat' (success)
    :t wait-for switched-scratch (success)
    :$ cat switch-name (exit: 0)

```stdout
scratch
```

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}:#{window_index}' (success)

```
scratch:0
```

    :t switch-client -t runner (success)
    :pane runner:0.0

If checkout creation fails, switching should fail without printing a session
name.

    :$ smth --base alpha --onto missing --switch invalid (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: error running 'jj workspace add': Created workspace in "alpha.invalid"
Error: Revision `missing` doesn't exist
```

A plain switch without a name is invalid, picker controls are rejected, and
switch is mutually exclusive with create.

    :$ smth --no-base --switch (exit: 1)

```stderr
error: a session name is required without a repository base
```

    :$ smth --no-base --switch scratch --query scratch (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--switch [<SESSION>]' cannot be used with '--query <STR>'

Usage: smth --no-base --switch [<SESSION>]

For more information, try 'help'.
```

    :$ smth --no-base --switch scratch --create scratch (exit: 2)

```stderr
error: the argument '--switch [<SESSION>]' cannot be used with '--create [<SESSION>]'

Usage: smth --no-base --switch [<SESSION>]

For more information, try 'help'.
```

